      <dict>
        <key>construction</key>
        <string>Keep the native closed-omega lower lobes, central defining stroke and lower-zone points. Translate the upper cap to the genuine same-cut rounded SC top; interpolate only the middle-zone control-point displacement with smoothstep, along the native italic axis. Upper cap and lower-lobe stroke geometry are not uniformly scaled. No ordinary Omega alias, reduced capital or reference outline.</string>
        <key>designBoundary</key>
        <string>Two-cut source hypothesis. A moved control-point field is not a C1 curve guarantee. Width, native lower-case versus SC stroke weights, central-stroke proportion, upper curvature, spacing and all-cut consistency require actual design review before a source target or route is accepted.</string>
